# MU300: no failsafe mode. OpenWrt's failsafe_wait (30_failsafe_wait) gives the serial console
# fs_failsafe_wait_timeout seconds to have "f" typed on it - on a device whose UART only test pads reach, that is
# seconds of every boot for nothing. Recovery here is the bootloader's (a Linux slot that does not come up is left for
# Android after its tries). Sourced after 30_failsafe_wait, so this is the definition its hook runs.
failsafe_wait() {
	FAILSAFE=
	return 0
}
# ...and no failsafe address: preinit_ip would run board_detect (0.9 s) to put 192.168.1.1 on usb0 for a failsafe
# nobody can enter, and run_init would then flush usb0's addresses and take it down - the early DHCP server's address
# with them (06_mu300_early_usb). With this set, preinit_ip returns at once and run_init leaves usb0 alone.
pi_preinit_no_failsafe="y"
